---
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/breadcrumbs.astro'
import Link from '@/components/link.astro'
import PageHead from '@/components/page-head.astro'
import Layout from '@/layouts/layout.astro'
import { formatDate } from '@/lib/utils'

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-04-01')
---

<Layout class="max-w-3xl">
  <PageHead slot="head" title="About" />

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-10">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About', icon: 'lucide:info' }]} />

      <header class="flex flex-col gap-3 border-b border-border pb-8">
        <h1
          class="text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight lowercase sm:text-4xl"
        >
          about
        </h1>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-lg font-medium">
          Some more about me
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">
          Last updated: {formatDate(lastUpdated)}
        </p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <article class="prose max-w-none">
      <p class="mt-0">
        I build at the intersection of AI, security, and tools people actually
        use day to day. A lot of what I care about is making powerful ideas
        usable—whether that is multi-user platforms, safer defaults for AI
        systems, or creative workflows that do not require a PhD to operate.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is where I ship in public: project notes, experiments, and
        longer write-ups when something is worth unpacking. You will see that
        mix on the <Link href="/" underline>home</Link> page and in the <Link
          href="/blog"
          underline>blog</Link
        >—from infrastructure-heavy work to problems I hit while editing drone
        footage and trying to fix audio that should have been easy.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am also interested in how the industry agrees on secure AI practices,
        which is part of why I pay attention to initiatives like the <Link
          href="https://www.coalitionforsecureai.org"
          external
          underline>Coalition for Secure AI</Link
        >. If something here resonates or you want to collaborate, the best
        starting point is still this site or the links I keep up to date on the
        homepage.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
